<title>USA: Freeport Copper buys back 18.2 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Freeport Copper buys back 18.2 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freeport-McMoRan Copper &amp; Gold Inc said Tuesday it has repurchased 18.2 million common shares under its previously announced open market share purchase program for up to 20 million shares.</p>
<p>The company said it repurchased 1.8 million shares during the second quarter for $49.9 million, about $28 per share.</p>
<p>From July 1 through July 21, the company said, it repurchased 2.8 million shares for $74.0 million, about $27 per share.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
